cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "poliwatch"
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite it using these metadata. The data is licensed in layers, one per source (ADR 0003, docs/adr/0003-licences-and-impressum.md); every data release states them in its DATA.md. A release has a version (calendar version YYYY.MM.DD, tag data-<version>) that you should name in the citation."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Veh"
    given-names: "Luca"
abstract: "A dataset and static site of Bundestag plenary proceedings: sittings, agenda items, speeches, roll-call votes and members, built from DIP, the Plenarprotokoll XML and bundestag.de. The code is MIT-licensed. The data is not under one licence: DIP-derived data keeps the DIP terms of use, roll-call data follows the Bundestag, abgeordnetenwatch profile data is CC0 1.0, and our own derived work is CC BY 4.0 (ADR 0003). The product name is not final; the title will change."
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Bundestag
  - parliament
  - open data
  - plenary protocols
  - roll-call votes
